 ~/.joerc: Joe's Own Editor
 Lines that start with a space are comments; options start in column 1.

 No backup files (file~)
-nobackups

 Defaults for every file: no word wrap, syntax highlighting,
 indent step 4, tab width 4
--wordwrap
-highlight
-istep 4
-tab 4

 Everything else (key bindings, menus, file types) comes from the stock
 config, so it stays current when joe is upgraded.  The file type table is
 read from ~/.joe/ftyperc, which is the stock table without its "-wordwrap"
 lines.  These options must stay above the include to apply to all types.
:include /opt/homebrew/etc/joe/joerc
